<hr class="border-border-l2">
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Entropy as Infrastructure</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">A Categorical and Bioeconomic Framework for Useful Computation as Heat, Semantic Merging, and Polycomputational Agency</p>
<hr class="border-border-l2">
<ol dir="auto" class="marker:text-secondary">
<li class="break-words">Introduction</li>
</ol>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Framing statement: Entropy is not a byproduct â€” it is the substrate of infrastructure.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Outline of the dual thesis:</p>
<ol dir="auto" class="marker:text-secondary">
<li class="break-words">Computation is an entropic process whose heat can be repurposed for environmental regulation.</li>
<li class="break-words">Semantic infrastructure, built on categorical formalisms, enables useful computation to be allocated, merged, and validated across contexts.</li>
</ol>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Critique of wasteful entropy generation (e.g., crypto mining for blockchain speculation) vs. productive entropy generation (useful computation-for-heat).</p>
<hr class="border-border-l2">
<ol dir="auto" class="marker:text-secondary" start="2">
<li class="break-words">Categorical Foundations for Semantic Infrastructure</li>
</ol>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Fibered Symmetric Monoidal Categories as the backbone for cross-domain computational objects.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Semantic modules  and entropy-respecting morphisms.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Homotopy colimits as semantic merge operators ensuring coherence across domains and time.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">RSVP field mapping:  (scalar semantic density),  (computational flow),  (entropy flux).</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Polycomputation formalism: multiple computational paradigms represented in a shared categorical framework.</p>
<hr class="border-border-l2">
<ol dir="auto" class="marker:text-secondary" start="3">
<li class="break-words">CLIO Module and Polycomputational Agency</li>
</ol>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">CLIO (Cognitive Loop via In-Situ Optimization) as a recursive inference functor in the RSVP category.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">How CLIO mediates inference task allocation across heterogeneous compute nodes.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Polycomputational agency: concurrent specialized modules (e.g., physics constant extraction, compression, environmental simulation) coordinated via semantic merge.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Example: detecting Earth climate anomalies from distributed sensor networks while simultaneously regulating habitat heat.</p>
<hr class="border-border-l2">
<ol dir="auto" class="marker:text-secondary" start="4">
<li class="break-words">Bioeconomic Thermoregulation</li>
</ol>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Earth context:</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Replacing heaters and heat pumps with high-performance compute clusters (GPUs, TPUs, and exotic architectures like cymatic yogurt computers).</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Waste heat used for building thermoregulation.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Computation tasks include compression research, LIDAR classification, environmental simulation, and quine generation.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Post-Earth context (Lunar &amp; beyond):</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Why blockchain-mining-heaters are wasteful.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Proposal: lunar heater-computers dedicated to environmental simulation, change magnification analysis, and error-checking research archives.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Funding models via public research objects and cooperative computation networks.</p>
