<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">The category of semantic modules, <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="bold">S</mi><mi mathvariant="bold">e</mi><mi mathvariant="bold">m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex"> \mathbf{Sem} </annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6861em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathbf">Sem</span></span></span></span></span>, is fibered over a base category <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="bold">D</mi><mi mathvariant="bold">o</mi><mi mathvariant="bold">m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex"> \mathbf{Dom} </annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6861em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathbf">Dom</span></span></span></span></span> of theoretical domains (e.g., RSVP cosmology, AI alignment). The projection functor <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>Ï€</mi><mo>:</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="bold">S</mi><mi mathvariant="bold">e</mi><mi mathvariant="bold">m</mi></mrow><mo>â†’</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="bold">D</mi><mi mathvariant="bold">o</mi><mi mathvariant="bold">m</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex"> \pi: \mathbf{Sem} \to \mathbf{Dom} </annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4306em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">Ï€</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">:</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-rig