</span></div><div style="position: absolute; top: 0px; left: 0px; width: 100%; height: 1.5em; transform: translateY(1944px);"><span><span>Bioeconomic thermoregulation replaces heaters with compute clusters (GPUs, TPUs, cymatic yogurt computers) </span><span style="color: rgb(198, 120, 221);">\citep</span><span>{Bennett1982, SagawaUeda2009}. Waste heat thermoregulates buildings, supporting computations like compression, LIDAR classification, environmental simulations, and quine generation </span><span style="color: rgb(198, 120, 221);">\citep</span><span>{Wolfram2002}. This aligns with ecological sustainability </span><span style="color: rgb(198, 120, 221);">\citep</span><span>{CapraLuisi2014, MargulisSagan1995}.
